hubble                package:AA                     R Documentation

Space Telescope Science Institute Employment Data

Description:

     The 'hubble' data frame has 2 rows and 3 columns.

     Employment of men and women at the Space Telescope Science
     Institute at Baltimore, which manages the Hubble Space Telescope. 
     Five of the seven women scientists hired in the period 1998-2002
     left within that period, while only one of 19 men hired in that
     period did so.

Usage:

     data(hubble)

Format:

     This data frame contains the following columns:

     'r' the number of employees who left in the period 1998-2002;

     'm' the total number of employees hired in the period 1998-2002;

     'x' a factor variable for gender (0 = male, 1 = female).

Source:

     The data were obtained from

     _Science_, Volume *299* (14 February 2003), Page 993.

References:

     Brazzale, A.R., Davison, A.C. and Reid, N. (2007).  _Applied 
     Asymptotics: Case Studies in Small-Sample Statistics_.  Cambridge 
     University Press, Cambridge.  Example 3.4.
